IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ddtr-dates`

-- Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019 (NSW), Part 5 -- offers of compromise, from the seat of the plaintiff (cl 87:
-- "plaintiff includes a cross-claimant"). Part 5 applies to all claims in the Tribunal, not only asbestos claims (the Note
-- to cl 86).
--
-- Provisions: cl 87 (period for acceptance, final deadline), cl 88(2), (4)-(6), (9), cl 89, 90 (costs after a rejected
-- offer), cl 92(1), cl 93 (withdrawing an acceptance), cl 94(2) (a defendant who does not comply). Out: cl 91 (interest
-- disregarded when comparing: folded into the comparison the person states), cl 95, 96 (disclosure to the Tribunal), and
-- the defendant's side of cl 94(1).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019, Part 5 -- offers of compromise`

§§ `The nouns`

DECLARE `Where my claim stands for offers` IS ONE OF
    `in the claims resolution process, before the required information exchange`
    `in the claims resolution process, after the exchange and before mediation has concluded`
    `after mediation under the claims resolution process has concluded`
    `removed from the claims resolution process under clause 20, before an Issues and Listing Conference`
    `removed from the claims resolution process under clause 20, after an Issues and Listing Conference`
    `never in the claims resolution process (not an asbestos claim, or pending before 1 September 2019)`

DECLARE `Who made the offer` IS ONE OF
    `I did`
    `the defendant did`

DECLARE `How my judgment compares with the offer` IS ONE OF
    `more favourable to me than the offer`
    `as favourable to me as the offer`
    `less favourable to me than the offer`

DECLARE `The costs after a rejected offer` IS ONE OF
    `cl 89: your costs, on the party and party basis up to the start of the day after the offer and on the indemnity basis from then`
    `cl 89: your costs, on the party and party basis up to 11 am on the day after the offer and on the indemnity basis from then`
    `cl 90: your costs on the party and party basis up to the start of the day after the offer; the defendant's costs, on the indemnity basis, from then`
    `cl 90: your costs on the party and party basis up to 11 am on the day after the offer; the defendant's costs, on the indemnity basis, from then`
    `the Tribunal ordered otherwise, in an exceptional case to avoid substantial injustice, and must give its reasons`
    `cl 89 does not apply: your judgment is less favourable to you than your offer`
    `cl 90 does not apply: your judgment is more favourable to you than the defendant's offer`
    `cl 89 and 90 do not apply: the offer was accepted (cl 92)`

DECLARE `Whether I can withdraw my acceptance` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the money was not paid, or the act not done, within the time (cl 93(1)(a))`
    `yes: the Tribunal granted leave (cl 93(1)(b))`
    `not yet: the time for payment or performance has not ended`
    `no: it was paid or done in time; only with the Tribunal's leave (cl 93(1)(b))`

DECLARE `Offer party` IS ONE OF
    `the defendant who must pay`
    `the plaintiff who accepted`

DECLARE `Offer act` IS ONE OF
    `pay the money or do the act the accepted offer provides`
    `withdraw the acceptance`

§§ `cl 88(4), (5) -- the shortest time an offer can be left open`

-- cl 88(4) for a claim (other than one removed under cl 20), the time "cannot be less than-- (a) 28 days after the offer is
-- made if the offer is made before the required information exchange under Part 3, or (b) 14 days ... after the required
-- information exchange ... but before mediation ... has been concluded, or (c) 7 days ... after mediation ... has been
-- concluded." (5) for a claim removed under cl 20: "(a) 14 days after the offer is made, unless paragraph (b) applies, or
-- (b) if the offer is made after an Issues and Listing Conference has been held ..., 7 days".
@export If I make an offer of compromise in the Dust Diseases Tribunal and limit how long it is open, what is the shortest time (in days) I can give (cl 88(4), (5))?
GIVEN `where my claim stands` IS A `Where my claim stands for offers` @desc Where the claim is when the offer is made: in the claims resolution process before or after the information exchange; after mediation concluded; removed from the process under clause 20, before or after an Issues and Listing Conference; or never in the process
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the shortest time my offer can be open` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where my claim stands`
    WHEN `in the claims resolution process, before the required information exchange` THEN JUST 28
    WHEN `in the claims resolution process, after the exchange and before mediation has concluded` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `after mediation under the claims resolution process has concluded` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `removed from the claims resolution process under clause 20, before an Issues and Listing Conference` THEN JUST 14
    WHEN `removed from the claims resolution process under clause 20, after an Issues and Listing Conference` THEN JUST 7
    WHEN `never in the claims resolution process (not an asbestos claim, or pending before 1 September 2019)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (cl 88(4) is framed on Part 3's stages; read literally it would give 28 days; fork F10)

§§ `cl 87 -- the period for acceptance`

-- cl 87 "period for acceptance for an offer means the period from when the offer is made until-- (a) the expiration of the
-- time limited by the offer or, if no time is limited, the expiration of 28 days after the offer is made, or (b) the final
-- deadline for offers in respect of the claim to which the offer relates, whichever first occurs." "final deadline ...
-- means the time at which the Tribunal begins to give its decision or its reasons for decision, whichever is the earlier".
@export Until what day can this offer of compromise in my Dust Diseases Tribunal claim be accepted (cl 87, 92(1))?
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the offer was made
      `the offer limits its time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer says how long it is open
      `days the offer is open` IS A NUMBER @desc If it does, how many days after it is made it stays open (otherwise any number)
      `the Tribunal has begun to give its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has begun (or has a date to begin) giving its decision or reasons on the claim
      `the day the Tribunal begins its decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal begins giving its decision or its reasons, whichever is earlier (any date if not)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when can the offer be accepted` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal has begun to give its decision` AND DATE_SERIAL `the day the Tribunal begins its decision` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the offer's own end`
    THEN `the day the Tribunal begins its decision`
    ELSE `the offer's own end`
    WHERE
        `the offer's own end` MEANS
            IF `the offer limits its time`
            THEN `the day the offer was made` `plus calendar days` `days the offer is open`
            ELSE `the day the offer was made` `plus calendar days` 28

§§ `cl 89, 90 -- costs after an offer that was not accepted`

-- cl 89(1) "This clause applies if the offer concerned is made by the plaintiff, but not accepted by the defendant, and the
-- plaintiff obtains an order or judgment on the claim concerned no less favourable to the plaintiff than the terms of the
-- offer." (2) "Unless the Tribunal orders otherwise in an exceptional case and for the avoidance of substantial
-- injustice", costs on the party and party basis, then on the indemnity basis "(i) if the offer was made before the first
-- day of the trial, as from the beginning of the day following the day on which the offer was made, and (ii) if the
-- offer was made on or after the first day of the trial, as from 11 am on the day following". cl 90 is the mirror for the
-- defendant's offer, where the judgment is "as favourable to the plaintiff, or less favourable". cl 91: interest for the
-- period after the offer is disregarded in the comparison; the person states the comparison with that done.
@export An offer of compromise in my Dust Diseases Tribunal claim was not accepted and judgment has been given: what costs order follows (cl 89, 90)?
GIVEN `who made the offer` IS A `Who made the offer` @desc Whether you (the plaintiff or cross-claimant) or the defendant made the offer
      `the offer was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer was accepted
      `how my judgment compares` IS A `How my judgment compares with the offer` @desc How your judgment compares with the offer's terms, leaving out interest for the time after the offer was made (cl 91)
      `the offer was made before the first day of the trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer was made before the first day of the trial
      `the Tribunal ordered otherwise in an exceptional case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal ordered otherwise, in an exceptional case and to avoid substantial injustice
GIVETH A `The costs after a rejected offer`
`What costs order follows the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer was accepted`
    THEN `cl 89 and 90 do not apply: the offer was accepted (cl 92)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `who made the offer`
         WHEN `I did` THEN
             CONSIDER `how my judgment compares`
             WHEN `less favourable to me than the offer` THEN `cl 89 does not apply: your judgment is less favourable to you than your offer`
             OTHERWISE
                 IF `the Tribunal ordered otherwise in an exceptional case`
                 THEN `the Tribunal ordered otherwise, in an exceptional case to avoid substantial injustice, and must give its reasons`
                 ELSE IF `the offer was made before the first day of the trial`
                      THEN `cl 89: your costs, on the party and party basis up to the start of the day after the offer and on the indemnity basis from then`
                      ELSE `cl 89: your costs, on the party and party basis up to 11 am on the day after the offer and on the indemnity basis from then`
         WHEN `the defendant did` THEN
             CONSIDER `how my judgment compares`
             WHEN `more favourable to me than the offer` THEN `cl 90 does not apply: your judgment is more favourable to you than the defendant's offer`
             OTHERWISE
                 IF `the Tribunal ordered otherwise in an exceptional case`
                 THEN `the Tribunal ordered otherwise, in an exceptional case to avoid substantial injustice, and must give its reasons`
                 ELSE IF `the offer was made before the first day of the trial`
                      THEN `cl 90: your costs on the party and party basis up to the start of the day after the offer; the defendant's costs, on the indemnity basis, from then`
                      ELSE `cl 90: your costs on the party and party basis up to 11 am on the day after the offer; the defendant's costs, on the indemnity basis, from then`

§§ `cl 88(6), 93 -- payment under an accepted offer, and withdrawing the acceptance`

-- cl 88(6) "Unless the notice of offer otherwise provides, an offer providing for the payment of money, or the doing of any
-- other act, is taken to provide for the payment of that money, or the doing of that act, within 28 days after acceptance
-- of the offer." cl 93(1) "A party who accepts an offer may withdraw the acceptance in either of the following
-- circumstances ...-- (a) if ... the sum is not paid to the party who accepts the offer or into the Tribunal, or the act
-- is not done, within 28 days after acceptance of the offer or within any other time as the offer provides, (b) if the
-- Tribunal grants the party leave to withdraw the acceptance." The duty to pay is written as a MUST whose LEST opens the
-- accepting party's permission to withdraw.
GIVEN `days to pay` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Offer party` `Offer act`
`the accepted offer must be paid within` `days to pay` MEANS
    PARTY `the defendant who must pay`
    MUST `pay the money or do the act the accepted offer provides`
    WITHIN `days to pay`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the plaintiff who accepted`
        MAY `withdraw the acceptance`

@export I accepted the defendant's offer of compromise: can I withdraw my acceptance on this day (cl 88(6), 93(1))?
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE @desc The day you served your notice of acceptance
      `the offer sets its own time to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offer says when the money is to be paid (or the act done)
      `days the offer allows to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc If it does, how many days after acceptance (otherwise any number)
      `it has been paid or done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money has been paid to you or into the Tribunal, or the act done
      `the day it was paid or done` IS A DATE @desc The day it was paid or done (any date if not)
      `the day I would withdraw` IS A DATE @desc The day you would serve notice withdrawing your acceptance
      `the Tribunal granted me leave to withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has granted you leave to withdraw the acceptance
GIVETH A `Whether I can withdraw my acceptance`
`Can I withdraw my acceptance` MEANS
    IF `paid within the time`
    THEN IF `the Tribunal granted me leave to withdraw`
         THEN `yes: the Tribunal granted leave (cl 93(1)(b))`
         ELSE `no: it was paid or done in time; only with the Tribunal's leave (cl 93(1)(b))`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the accepted offer must be paid within` `the days to pay`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the withdrawal time`), EVENT `the plaintiff who accepted` `withdraw the acceptance` `the withdrawal time`)
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `yes: the money was not paid, or the act not done, within the time (cl 93(1)(a))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the Tribunal granted me leave to withdraw`
             THEN `yes: the Tribunal granted leave (cl 93(1)(b))`
             ELSE `not yet: the time for payment or performance has not ended`
    WHERE
        `the days to pay` MEANS IF `the offer sets its own time to pay` THEN `days the offer allows to pay` ELSE 28
        `the withdrawal time` MEANS `the calendar days from` `the day I accepted` `until` `the day I would withdraw`
        `paid within the time` MEANS
            IF `it has been paid or done`
            THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the accepted offer must be paid within` `the days to pay`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the defendant who must pay` `pay the money or do the act the accepted offer provides` (`the calendar days from` `the day I accepted` `until` `the day it was paid or done`)))
                 WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE
            ELSE FALSE

§§ `cl 94(2) -- a defendant who does not comply with an accepted offer`

DECLARE `What I may elect when the defendant does not comply` IS ONE OF
    `you may elect either judgment or orders giving effect to the accepted offer, or that the defence be struck out and judgment entered (cl 94(2)), unless the Tribunal orders otherwise`
    `cl 94(2) does not arise: the defendant has not failed to comply`

-- cl 94(2) "If the defendant, being a party to an accepted offer, fails to comply with the terms of the offer, the
-- plaintiff is entitled to either of the following as the plaintiff elects, unless the Tribunal orders otherwise-- (a)
-- any judgment or order as is appropriate to give effect to the terms of the accepted offer, (b) an order that the
-- defence be struck out, and to judgment accordingly."
@export The defendant has not complied with an offer of compromise I accepted: what am I entitled to (cl 94(2))?
GIVEN `the defendant failed to comply with the accepted offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant failed to comply with the terms of the offer you accepted
GIVETH A `What I may elect when the defendant does not comply`
`What can I do if the defendant does not comply` MEANS
    IF `the defendant failed to comply with the accepted offer`
    THEN `you may elect either judgment or orders giving effect to the accepted offer, or that the defence be struck out and judgment entered (cl 94(2)), unless the Tribunal orders otherwise`
    ELSE `cl 94(2) does not arise: the defendant has not failed to comply`
